            <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Stores combining ecommerce with sales follow-up or B2B workflows</td><td>Stores needing advanced popups, quizzes, and onsite capture</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Pricing</td><td>From ~$29/mo</td><td>From ~$29/mo</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Shopify depth</td><td>Integration</td><td>Native</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Automation</td><td>Advanced</td><td>Minimal</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cart channels</td><td>email, marketing</td><td>marketing</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rating</td><td>4.5/5</td><td>4.5/5</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p>These are proposed test scenarios and illustrative calculations, not observed supplier results. Contribution equals AOV × (gross margin rate − discount rate), assuming fixed product cost; discount loss equals AOV × discount rate, before messaging, shipping, taxes, returns and other variable costs. Timings below are separate test variants, not a combined send schedule. Justuno capture and a connected sender require separate capability and permission checks; channel suggestions do not establish either product’s sending support. Before each send, the queue owner must recheck current purchase, stock and suppression state, purpose-specific permission and quiet hours, and deduplicate replayed events.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: scenario 1 — international shipping quote sticker shock. At $644 AOV and 63% margin, full-price recovery contributes $405.72 vs $354.20 after a 8% code (Δ $51.52). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for duplicate SMS and email within 20 minutes. Email 1 ~30m, email 2 ~47h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: scenario 2 — subscription toggle left on at checkout. At $644 AOV and 63% margin, full-price recovery contributes $405.72 vs $354.20 after a 8% code (Δ $51.52). Ladder touch 2 favors email proof; watch for welcome discount stacking with cart code. Email 1 ~30m, email 2 ~47h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: scenario 3 — first-time mobile shopper on Instagram traffic. At $644 AOV and 63% margin, full-price recovery contributes $405.72 vs $354.20 after a 8% code (Δ $51.52). Ladder touch 3 favors SMS urgency; watch for discount on email one before trust proof. Email 1 ~30m, email 2 ~47h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: scenario 4 — size matrix with two variants OOS. At $644 AOV and 63% margin, full-price recovery contributes $405.72 vs $354.20 after a 8% code (Δ $51.52). Ladder touch 4 favors push nudge; watch for SMS after 9pm local without quiet hours. Email 1 ~30m, email 2 ~47h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
        <p>ActiveCampaign vs Justuno: scenario 5 — gift message field abandoned mid-flow. At $644 AOV and 63% margin, full-price recovery contributes $405.72 vs $354.20 after a 8% code (Δ $51.52). Ladder touch 1 favors no-discount assist; watch for no suppression after partial refund. Email 1 ~30m, email 2 ~47h, SMS branch ~6h for opted-in only.</p>
